Review the uncommitted stmap3 AutoEDA iteration in this ABC repository.

Binding project context:
- New command should be stmap3 and preserve map, stmap0, stmap1, and stmap2 behavior.
- Hypothesis: during mapper area recovery, reject high-fanout wide cuts only when the current mapper match has a shallow positive slack window, so near-critical fanout/load choices are protected while very noncritical nodes remain available for area recovery.
- Required correctness gates already run locally: make ABC_USE_NO_READLINE=1, stmap3 -h, i10 smoke, four benchmark baseline/candidate flows, and CEC for i10/ode/or1200/syn2.
